---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy Policy — EmailSubjectScore Pro"
  description="Privacy policy for EmailSubjectScore Pro. Learn what information is used to provide scoring and how your privacy is protected."
  canonical="https://amrita-labs.com/gmail-subject-score/privacy/"
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-24 prose prose-invert prose-sm">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white">Privacy Policy — EmailSubjectScore Pro</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-gray-400"><strong>Effective Date</strong>: 2026-05-18 · <strong>Last Updated</strong>: 2026-08-15</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">1. Who We Are</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300">EmailSubjectScore Pro is operated by Amrita Labs.<br />Contact: <a href="mailto:hello@amrita-labs.com" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">hello@amrita-labs.com</a></p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">2. What This Extension Does</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300">EmailSubjectScore Pro scores email subject lines as you type in Gmail compose, providing spam, clarity, and urgency ratings with AI-powered rewrite suggestions.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">3. Data We Collect</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300">We collect <strong>only</strong> the following:</p>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="text-sm text-gray-300 w-full">
        <thead><tr class="border-b border-white/10"><th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Category</th><th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">What</th><th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Why</th><th class="text-left py-2">Retention</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Anonymous device ID</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Random UUID generated on install</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Rate limiting &amp; free-tier cap</td><td class="py-2">Until deletion request</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Aggregated usage events</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Counts of feature uses</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Product improvement</td><td class="py-2">Up to 24 months</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="py-2 pr-4">Error logs</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Stack traces (no user content)</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Bug fixing</td><td class="py-2">Up to 90 days</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-gray-300 mt-4">We do <strong>NOT</strong> collect:</p>
    <ul class="text-gray-300">
      <li>Email message bodies or recipients</li>
      <li>Page contents beyond the subject line you choose to score</li>
      <li>Browsing history</li>
      <li>Any personally identifiable information without explicit account creation</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">4. What Leaves Your Browser</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300">When you request a score or rewrite, the extension sends only what is needed to provide that requested feature:</p>
    <ul class="text-gray-300">
      <li>Anonymous device ID (no name, no email)</li>
      <li>The subject line text you choose to process</li>
      <li>Limited diagnostic metadata, such as extension version</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-gray-300">Subject line text is used only to provide the requested scoring or rewrite feature and is not intentionally retained after processing. We may use service providers to process requests on our behalf under appropriate safeguards.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">5. Third-Party Services</h2>
    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="text-sm text-gray-300 w-full">
        <thead><tr class="border-b border-white/10"><th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Service</th><th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Data shared</th><th class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Purpose</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4">AI processing providers</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Subject line text when you request scoring or rewriting</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Provide requested scoring and rewrite features</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Hosting and service providers</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Encrypted service requests and limited technical data</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Operate and secure the service</td></tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-white/5"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Analytics providers</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Anonymous usage events</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Understand feature use and improve reliability</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="py-2 pr-4">Error-reporting providers</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Limited error diagnostics</td><td class="py-2 pr-4">Identify and fix technical issues</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="text-gray-300 mt-4">We do <strong>NOT</strong> sell, share, or rent your data to advertisers or data brokers.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">6. Your Rights</h2>
    <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-white mt-6">GDPR (EU users)</h3>
    <ul class="text-gray-300">
      <li>Right to access, rectify, erase, restrict, or port your data</li>
      <li>Right to object to processing</li>
      <li>Right to lodge a complaint with your supervisory authority</li>
    </ul>
    <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-white mt-6">CCPA / CPRA (California users)</h3>
    <ul class="text-gray-300">
      <li>Right to know what we collect</li>
      <li>Right to delete</li>
      <li>Right to opt out of "sale" or "sharing" — we do not sell or share your data</li>
      <li>Right to non-discrimination</li>
    </ul>
    <h3 class="text-lg font-medium text-white mt-6">PIPEDA (Canadian users)</h3>
    <ul class="text-gray-300">
      <li>Right to know what personal information we hold and how it is used</li>
      <li>Right to access and challenge accuracy</li>
      <li>Right to withdraw consent at any time</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-gray-300 mt-4">For any rights request: <a href="mailto:hello@amrita-labs.com" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">hello@amrita-labs.com</a></p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">7. Data Retention &amp; Deletion</h2>
    <ul class="text-gray-300">
      <li>Anonymous identifiers and usage information: retained only as reasonably necessary for service operation, abuse prevention, and product improvement</li>
      <li>Error diagnostics: retained for a limited period appropriate to troubleshooting</li>
      <li>Subject text: not intentionally retained after the requested processing is complete</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">8. Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300">This extension is not intended for users under 13 (COPPA) or under 16 in the EU (GDPR). We do not knowingly collect data from children.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">9. Security</h2>
    <ul class="text-gray-300">
      <li>Reasonable technical and organizational safeguards protect information in transit and at rest</li>
      <li>Access to service systems is limited to what is needed to operate and support the extension</li>
      <li>Usage limits and abuse controls help protect the service</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">10. AI Disclosure</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300">This extension uses automated and AI-assisted processing to score subject lines and generate alternative suggestions. AI-generated content is identified in the interface and should be reviewed before use.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300">We may update this policy at any time. Material changes will be communicated via an in-extension banner and by updating the "Last Updated" date above. Continued use after changes constitutes acceptance.</p>

    <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white mt-10">12. Contact</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-300">For any privacy questions: <a href="mailto:hello@amrita-labs.com" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">hello@amrita-labs.com</a></p>
  </article>

  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 pb-12 flex gap-6 text-xs text-gray-500">
    <a href="/gmail-subject-score/" class="hover:text-gray-400">← Back to EmailSubjectScore Pro</a>
    <a href="/gmail-subject-score/terms/" class="hover:text-gray-400">Terms of Service</a>
  </div>
</Base>
